{
  "valuation_insights": "Costco Wholesale Corporation's fiscal 2026 fiscal year reported total revenue of $303.154 billion [C:revenue_current], while net sales stood at $297.247 billion as per release line 10, highlighting a $5.9 billion difference attributable to non-sales revenue components. The fiscal 2026 total revenue increased by 10.14% from $275.235 billion in fiscal 2025 [C:revenue_growth]. Operating income was $11.685 billion, generating an operating margin of 3.85% when computed against total revenue [C:operating_income_current][C:operating_margin]. Net income attributable to the company was $9.226 billion with GAAP diluted EPS of $20.76 [C:net_income_current][C:diluted_eps_current]. Return on average equity was strong at 28.40% [C:return_on_average_equity]. The debt-to-equity ratio, including current portion of long-term debt, was conservative at 0.172 [C:debt_to_equity]. Free cash flow totaled $9.382 billion, calculated as operating cash flow less capital expenditures [C:free_cash_flow].\n\nIn the latest fiscal quarter (16 weeks ended August 30, 2026), net sales were $93.9 billion, up 11.2% compared to the same quarter last year, according to release line 10 [C:quarterly_revenue_growth]. The quarter's GAAP diluted EPS was $6.75 [C:quarterly_diluted_eps]. With a stock price of $904.7 as of September 23, 2026, the price-to-earnings ratio is approximately 43.58 [C:price_to_earnings].\n\nComparing Costco's operating margin of 3.85% (using total revenue) to peers: Walmart had 4.18%, Target 4.88%, and BJ's Wholesale Club 3.81%, all derived from their respective XBRL data [C:peer_operating_margins]. This positions Costco marginally below Walmart and Target but slightly above BJ's Wholesale Club.\n\nInsight: Cost control improvements and favorable debt reduction were notable in fiscal 2026, as evidenced by a decrease in long-term non-current debt from $5.713 billion to $3.914 billion, complemented by positive free cash flow generation, enhancing Costco's financial flexibility beyond its expanding international warehouse footprint [L:10-K line 21].",
